Target model: Krea 2. Describe exactly what you want to see in plain natural language, with the subject and concrete lighting ahead of supporting detail. Keep the setting sparse: every additional named object has to be lit to be visible, so an inventoried background is what talks this model out of the lighting you described and into a flat, evenly-lit frame — name only the props the moment actually needs. State exclusions positively: describe the visible emptiness of a place the concept already names, rather than writing a negation about what is absent — a negated clause reads to this model as if it were absent, so what it excludes comes back.

